cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Pyzed in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Pyzed: native desktop GUIs in Python, rendered by Iced (Rust)"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: albakore
abstract: >-
  Pyzed is an open-source Python frontend framework for native desktop apps. Python describes the interface and
  Iced, a GPU-accelerated GUI toolkit written in Rust, lays it out and draws it. It ships 90+ components inspired
  by the Zed editor, themes, animations, node-based GPU shaders, packaging for Windows, macOS and Linux and
  Pyzed Design, a drag-and-drop visual designer. Published on PyPI as pyzed-ui.
url: "https://albakore.github.io/pyzed/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/albakore/pyzed"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - python
  - gui
  - desktop
  - rust
  - iced
  - gui-framework
  - visual-designer
  - cross-platform
